# Spec-driven changes

Any code change belongs to an active OpenSpec change under `openspec/changes/<name>/`. If none exists, create one with `/openspec-propose` before editing Kotlin, Gradle, or `openspec/specs/`. The same step answers to “opsx propose”.

Cycle: propose → implement `tasks.md` (`/openspec-apply-change`) → `:app:testDebugUnitTest` → `/openspec-archive-change`. Do not archive while tests fail. Do not edit `openspec/specs/` by hand; archive merges the delta. Skills live in `.agents/skills/`.

Mission intent: `spec/mission.md`. Shipped contracts: `openspec/specs/`. Preservation baselines are the task list, the flow session, and the day dial.

```text
# ❌ BAD — patch DayViewModel with no change folder
# ✅ GOOD — /opsx-propose fix-pause-checkpoint, then edit, test, /opsx-archive
```

Before sending a file to the LLM, check `.cursorignore`. Agent, Tab, and `@` mentions skip those paths. The terminal and MCP do not. Do not add production keys to the working tree.
